#version 460
// THE SCREEN-PROBE GATHER, JOB 4 OF 4: BACK TO THE PIXELS
// (GATHER-1a; the plane-weighted SH integrate PHOTON-GATHER-1b item 3,
// SPECS/photon/C2_GATHER_FILTERED_DEFAULT_ON_DESIGN.md section 1.3).
//
// ONE THREAD PER PIXEL. The pixel reads the FOUR cells around it — bilinear in
// probe space, the cells whose centres bracket the pixel — each by its uniform
// probe or, where the cell has one and it agrees better, its ADAPTIVE twin
// (Lumen's corner rule), and weighs each by THE PLANE TEST (the pixel's
// distance off the probe's plane as a fraction of its own view distance, and
// the two normals' dot — jahPlaneWeight, the tolerances the placement job's
// adaptive test uses, as ramps). Each probe answers with its SH EVALUATED AT
// THE PIXEL'S OWN NORMAL, so the irradiance follows the surface the pixel is
// on, not the one the probe sat on. A twin carries its corner's bilinear share.
//
// WHAT THE PLANE WEIGHT DECIDES. A cell's probes describe the surfaces they
// sit on; a pixel belongs to the ones whose plane it lies in. Weighing by
// distance to the PLANE (and by normal agreement) rather than by distance in
// pixels is what keeps a bounce on the side of a silhouette it belongs to —
// "leaks confined to the plane", the property the whole probe shape exists for.
// A pixel whose weights sum below the floor (p.knobs4.y) gets NO answer and takes
// the FALLBACK — the irradiance field's cage where one is bound, at its confidence
// (where it fades, no sample: 10-3 R3) — composed HERE, after the
// temporal mean (PHOTON-7 stage 7, 7-2: the opaque passes read only screen
// products, L4; the field's reader is one text, jah_field_read.glsl).
//
// THE OUTPUT is `jahProbeIrradiance`: rgb = E/pi at the pixel's normal (what
// `envColourD` is — the trace's header): the answered frames' mean at their share
// plus the fallback's for the rest, and w = 1 - the pass that reads it binds no
// world cache (7-5). With no field bound rgb is the answered mean and w its
// coverage. A pixel gets exactly ONE diffuse-GI term in every regime.
//
// THE SECOND OUTPUT, `jahRoughSpec` (PHOTON-7 stage 7, 7-3; Lumen's rough
// reflections, the lead's ruling B): THE SPLIT SUM ON THE PROBES. The filter
// stores each probe's filtered radiance PREFILTERED by the GGX lobe at three
// roughnesses (p.roughLevels; rq_probe_filter.comp) - the convolution HlmsPbs's
// environment cube holds in its mips, on the probes' own hemispheres - and a
// pixel reads its bilinear probes (the diffuse's own taps and plane weights) along
// the lobe's DOMINANT direction (jahEnvDominantDir, the same fit at every
// environment reader), the two levels around its roughness lerped (below the
// first, the first: the 8 x 8 map resolves no sharper lobe). A probe whose
// hemisphere does not hold the direction says nothing and the rest renormalise;
// none holds it - the pixel's diffuse E/pi. A DETERMINISTIC READ OF THE PROBES -
// no draw: what noise it carries is the probes' own (each frame's trace), which
// only time removes, so the lobe takes THE DIFFUSE'S OWN HISTORY AND REST LAW
// (Lumen's RoughSpecularIndirect rides the diffuse's temporal pass): one shared-
// exponent word a pixel, read at the texel the diffuse's history accepted (one
// surface validation, one blend, the freeze and a starved frame keeping it), and
// at rest its own rest mean (R2: never seeded from the history, no sample under the
// freeze, the same hand-over). Then THE HAND-OVER TO THE DIFFUSE between the
// perceptual roughnesses p.rough.z and p.rough.w (Lumen's DiffuseLerp: the cosine
// lobe is the widest lobe). THE GATE (w): where the view's TRACED REFLECTION owns the lobe - below
// p.rough.x (its cutoff less its feather, the fork's SSR composite replacing the
// environment term at its confidence) - the reflection's own warm-up hands over to
// the material's cube as before, so w ramps from 0 at p.rough.x - p.rough.y to 1
// at p.rough.x (p.rough.x < 0: no traced reflection, w 1 everywhere). What the
// shading pass takes: envColourS += rgb x w, the cube x (1 - w); the cone's
// specular is compiled out of a pass that reads it (the sky arrives once).
//
// DETERMINISM: the five taps are read and summed in ONE FIXED ORDER.
//
// THE PIXEL HISTORY (PHOTON-GATHER-1c item 1; C2 design section 2). The answer
// above is one frame's estimate — 64 jittered rays a probe, a jittered probe a
// cell — and a pixel's irradiance is a quantity of its SURFACE POINT alone: the
// integrand E(x, n) = INTEGRAL L cos has no view vector in it, so the value at a
// world point does not change when the camera does. That is what makes a
// temporal mean at pixel resolution both possible and cheap: last frame's mean
// at THIS surface point is found through the previous camera
// (jah_reproject.glsl, rq_reflect.comp's arithmetic, one text), VALIDATED as
// the same surface — Lumen's rule (PHOTON-2 stage 2d, jah_probe_history.glsl):
// its stored distance within a jittered 1 % over NoV (3 % for foliage) and its
// stored surface class the same — and blended with this frame's estimate by the COUNT kept in the
// history (a true running mean while young, then a floor so it follows a
// changing scene). NEVER A NEIGHBOURHOOD CLAMP: a clamp to this frame's local
// range is a statement that the history is WRONG wherever it disagrees with
// one noisy frame, which throws away exactly the averaging the history exists
// for; the surface tests are the only rejection.
//
// WHAT THE HISTORY HOLDS, per pixel, in ONE PACKED TEXEL of 8 bytes, ping-ponged
// (a pixel reads the mean at its reprojected coordinate while its neighbours
// write theirs — one image would make that a race). PHOTON-GA-VR packed it from
// two images of 12 bytes (rgba16f + r32ui): 24 -> 16 bytes a pixel for the pair,
// one format for every view (a headset's 10.3 Mpx: 246 -> 164 MB).
//   .x  the mean of (E/pi x coverage) — PREMULTIPLIED, so a pixel a probe
//       answers on some frames and not others (the jittered probes, a plane
//       test at its tolerance) holds the answered frames' mean irradiance at the
//       FRACTION of frames that answered, and hands the rest to the fallback
//       smoothly instead of flickering between the two estimators frame by
//       frame; and a pixel no probe answers any more fades to the fallback at
//       the history's own rate — as a SHARED-EXPONENT 9-9-9-5 word (the
//       E5B9G9R9 layout, packed by hand because that format is not a storage
//       format): 9 bits of mantissa against the brightest channel.
//   .y  the surface's view distance (21 bits: a float's exponent and its top 13
//       mantissa bits, 0.006 % against the test's 0.5 % floor), its CLASS (1 bit:
//       foliage), the count (4 bits: the blend reads it only up to the floor,
//       1/10 shipped) and the mean COVERAGE (6 bits).
// THE ROUNDING OF THE TWO ACCUMULATED QUANTITIES IS STOCHASTIC (`roundingDither`,
// keyed on the view's ADVANCING frame counter): an EMA at a 1/10 blend stored
// round-to-nearest cannot move while a tenth of its innovation is under half a
// quantum, so it would stall up to five quanta from the mean it estimates (a
// coverage of 0.9 in 6 bits would never climb back to 1 once every frame
// answers); rounded up with probability equal to the fraction it is UNBIASED,
// and exact values (a coverage of 0 or 1, a zero) round to themselves. Measured
// against a deterministic "step one quantum toward the sample" rule, it adds
// less noise (gi.gather_motion's still control 0.215 against 0.232 codes).
// THE BUILDER'S NOTES (C2 design, section 2): the history is in IRRADIANCE
// space at the pixel — the atlas' re-weighting (note a) is inside the unbiased
// quadrature the SH was projected with, the atlas' hit distances (note b) never
// enter it (its distance is the SURFACE's), and the SH anchor (note c) is
// evaluated before it: the history averages E/pi, never coefficients.
//
// RULE 5 (PAN-SMEAR-1), point by point. (1) A pixel new to the screen — off the
// previous picture, behind the previous camera, reprojected onto a texel that
// held no surface — restarts its mean from this frame's estimate at FULL
// weight: there is no warm-up fade anywhere in this history (the ray tier's
// eight-frame fade exists because one GGX ray is not an estimate of a lobe; a
// gather pixel's first frame is a 9-probe, 576-ray filtered estimate), so no
// band can form on the side a pan turns toward. (2) The VIEW'S AGE (p.knobs5.x)
// decides whether the previous images hold anything at all — a first frame, a
// resize, a scene bind never read them. (3) "What the ray reached": a
// reflection's history must validate what it REFLECTS because the reflected
// point moves with the eye; a diffuse pixel's hemisphere does not depend on the
// eye, so the SURFACE test is the whole validation — the one view-dependent
// input left (the camera-centred cascades that shade a hit) moves by a cascade
// step, which is exactly what a temporal mean is for (gi.gather_motion measures
// the truck and the yaw).
#extension GL_GOOGLE_include_directive : require

layout( local_size_x = 8, local_size_y = 8, local_size_z = 1 ) in;

#define JAH_PROBE_PARAMS_BINDING 0
#include "jah_probe_params.glsl"

layout( std430, set = 0, binding = 1 ) readonly buffer Records { JahProbeRecord r[]; } records;
layout( set = 0, binding = 2 ) uniform sampler2DArray gBufNormals;
layout( set = 0, binding = 3 ) uniform sampler2DArray sceneDepth;
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 4 ) uniform image2DArray probeIrradiance;
/// THE PIXEL HISTORY, ping-ponged (see the header): the previous frame's texel,
/// read at the reprojected coordinate, and this frame's, written at this pixel.
layout( rg32ui, set = 0, binding = 5 ) uniform readonly uimage2DArray historyPrev;
layout( rg32ui, set = 0, binding = 6 ) uniform writeonly uimage2DArray historyCur;
/// THE REST MEAN (PHOTON-GATHER-1d): at rest — the camera, the lighting and the
/// scene held still (p.knobs6.x = the rest frame k >= 1) — a TRUE MEAN of the rest
/// frames' estimates, restarted at the first rest frame, premultiplied by
/// coverage like the history. The same pixel reads and writes it (the camera has
/// not moved, so there is no reprojection and no race): one image, not a pair.
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 7 ) uniform image2DArray restMean;
/// THE PHOTON VIEW'S OVERLAY (PHOTON-VIEW-1, binding 8): with p.knobs4.w = 1 (the
/// scene's view is ScreenProbes) every pixel writes whether it lies on one of the
/// probes around it — a disc at the probe's own position, coloured by the
/// irradiance its rays traced — or a dim veil. Written ONLY under the knob and read
/// by nothing here: the integrate's answer and its histories are the view's none
/// of its business. With the knob off the binding holds a stand-in, never written.
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 8 ) uniform writeonly image2DArray photonOverlay;
/// THE FRAME'S COUNTER (the placement's buffer, zeroed at the frame's head): word 1 counts the pixels whose history only
/// the foliage rule accepted (PHOTON-2 L8, K5's guard; read back with the placement's word 0); words 2 and 3 the pixels
/// that reached the HOLD with no rest sample - the diffuse's and the rough specular's (PHOTON-7 stage 10-3: they answer
/// NO SAMPLE there, below).
layout( std430, set = 0, binding = 9 ) buffer GatherCounter { uint words[]; } gatherCounter;
/// THE IRRADIANCE FIELD (PHOTON-7 stage 7, 7-2; bindings 10, 11): the fallback of the pixels no probe answers is the
/// field's cage at its confidence - jah_field_read.glsl, the one text the PBS pixel's reader runs too; where it fades,
/// no sample (10-3 R3) - composed into this texture AFTER the temporal mean (the history stays the gather's one
/// estimator): out = the history's premultiplied mean + ( 1 - its coverage ) x the fallback, w = 1 (the shading pass
/// binds no field, 7-5). p.fieldWin.w 0: no field bound - the coverage as w, no fallback.
layout( set = 0, binding = 10 ) uniform sampler2D fieldIrradiance;
layout( set = 0, binding = 11 ) uniform sampler2D fieldDepth;
#define JAH_FIELD_IRRAD( uv ) textureLod( fieldIrradiance, uv, 0.0 )
#define JAH_FIELD_DEPTH( uv ) textureLod( fieldDepth, uv, 0.0 ).xy
/// THE ROUGH SPECULAR (PHOTON-7 stage 7, 7-3; bindings 12 - 14 - the header's second output): the prepass's shadow /
/// roughness G-buffer (.y the GGX alpha, fork 16d8e29d4's packing over [0.001, 1]: rq_reflect.comp's decode), the
/// filter's PREFILTERED maps (one layer a roughness level, bilinear inside each probe's block) and the output.
layout( set = 0, binding = 12 ) uniform sampler2DArray gBufShadowRoughness;
layout( set = 0, binding = 13 ) uniform sampler2DArray prefilteredAtlas;
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 14 ) uniform writeonly image2DArray roughSpec;
/// ...the lobe's history pair (one shared-exponent word a pixel, at the diffuse history's texel) and its rest mean (a
/// 1 x 1 stand-in under stereo, as the diffuse's).
layout( r32ui, set = 0, binding = 15 ) uniform readonly uimage2DArray roughHistoryPrev;
layout( r32ui, set = 0, binding = 16 ) uniform writeonly uimage2DArray roughHistoryCur;
layout( rgba16f, set = 0, binding = 17 ) uniform image2DArray roughRest;
// (the environment's SH alone: no cube is read here)
#define JAH_ENV_CUBE_ON false
#define JAH_ENV_SAMPLE( d, l ) vec3( 0.0 )
#define JAH_ENV_MIPS 1.0
#define JAH_ENV_GAIN vec3( 0.0 )
#define JAH_ENV_SH_C0 p.envSh[0].xyz
#define JAH_ENV_SH_C1 p.envSh[1].xyz
#define JAH_ENV_SH_C2 p.envSh[2].xyz
#define JAH_ENV_SH_C3 p.envSh[3].xyz
#define JAH_ENV_SH_C4 p.envSh[4].xyz
#define JAH_ENV_SH_C5 p.envSh[5].xyz
#define JAH_ENV_SH_C6 p.envSh[6].xyz
#define JAH_ENV_SH_C7 p.envSh[7].xyz
#define JAH_ENV_SH_C8 p.envSh[8].xyz
#include "jah_environment.glsl"
#include "jah_field_window.glsl"
#include "jah_field_read.glsl"

// THE VOXEL CHAIN (PHOTON-7 10-3 R3 (b); L9: the renderer follows the ray): where the field's confidence fades, the
// share a probe did not answer is gathered by the world caches' rays (jah_voxel_cones.glsl's jahRayDiffuse at
// kJahPixelDiffuseRays - the no-ray route's screen integrate's one estimator), never the sky unoccluded and never
// nothing: the hit set's volumes by kind (bindings 18 - 24: the front, coverage +/-, position +/-, the back, the
// normal - what an occupancy ray reads), its uniforms the trace's (p.hit: the chain's boxes).
layout( set = 0, binding = 18 ) uniform sampler3D voxelIso[kMaxCascades];
layout( set = 0, binding = 19 ) uniform sampler3D voxelCovP[kMaxCascades];
layout( set = 0, binding = 20 ) uniform sampler3D voxelCovN[kMaxCascades];
layout( set = 0, binding = 21 ) uniform sampler3D voxelPosP[kMaxCascades];
layout( set = 0, binding = 22 ) uniform sampler3D voxelPosN[kMaxCascades];
layout( set = 0, binding = 23 ) uniform sampler3D voxelBack[kMaxCascades];
